a"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "28 July –  5 August 2012"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/872"} "North Greenwich Arena, Greenwich, London"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/313012"} "70 from 33 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Picking a favorite in the men’s gymnastics floor exercises at the 2012 Summer Olympics was a toss-up between " [:a {:href "/athletes/111925"} "Kohei Uchimura"] " of Japan and " [:a {:href "/athletes/111922"} "Zou Kai"] " of China. Uchimura was the three-time World Champion in the all-around, the reigning World Champion and 2010 runner-up in the floor exercises, and a newly minted Olympic Champion in the all-around. Zou was the defending Olympic champion and twice runner-up (2009 and 2011) at the World Championships in the floor exercises. In the qualification round, Zou finished ahead of Uchimura by 0.067 points, after a slightly poorer execution of a more difficult routine."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final Zou was the clear winner, defending his Olympic title with a score of 15.933. With 15.800 points Uchimura tied " [:a {:href "/athletes/120449"} "Denis Ablyazin"] " of Russia, who had the highest difficulty of 7.100, but the Japanese gymnast earned the silver medal by virtue of his higher execution score, 9.100 to 8.700. " [:a {:href "/athletes/121291"} "Enrique González"] " of Chile placed fourth, a notable result for a country that had never before participated in men’s Olympic gymnastics, while " [:a {:href "/athletes/111968"} "Aleksandr Shatilov"] " of Israel placed sixth, improving on his nation’s best Olympic gymnastics performance that he set in 2008, when he finished eighth in the same event."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "